The fork adds object checks, hover-detail commands and grouped metrics
with overview, carousel, horizontal and vertical displays. Standalone
metrics, whole groups and their main/child members can be disabled without
deleting their configuration. Unavailable-object visibility is configurable
for all displays, with a separate carousel-only setting.

Saved connection and layout scopes use stable local IDs, apply to both
display and collection, and match each pane independently in mixed layouts.
Removed targets never broaden a restricted scope to all panes.

Built-in CPU, memory, disk and network definitions are editable through the
same model as custom metrics. Per-item defaults can be restored. Both
panels use the common label display and persist the same configurable
built-in ordering. Inline editors, aligned hover rows, stable carousel
widths, section/card borders and compact group separators improve use.

The offline JSON library supports standalone and grouped presets, portable
connection-name bindings, import/export, bilingual descriptions and source
metadata. Adapted upstream presets retain their MIT source attribution.
Added presets include separate host/container disk groups, GPU memory
groups and CPU load groups. Optional GitHub import reads this fork's main
branch and merges library previews without activating downloaded commands.
Bundled disk groups aggregate valid unique filesystems, with the system
disk as their first child. Login-session details aggregate the system's
who records by username. Linux/macOS network metrics separate received
and sent rates and cumulative interface counters. Corresponding presets
also define consistent green, orange and red threshold rules.

The 26 added monitoring SVG icons are original artwork created for this
fork and are distributed under the same MIT license. The searchable icon
picker and interface support English and Chinese.

SSH output handling includes bounded completion acknowledgments; hover
detail caching follows each metric's refresh interval without automatically
rerunning user commands to recover missing output.

The SSH transport hotfix introduced in 1.6.1 is retained. Earlier oversized
exec requests could disconnect the shared SSH connection. A fixed short
exec request now streams scripts through standard input in 8 KiB chunks,
avoiding oversized packets and shell arguments. Completion acknowledgment
follows the full upload; transfer failures close only the statistics channel.

Third-party dependencies retain their respective licenses. Preserve any
license notice files emitted alongside the compiled files in dist/.
